<!--
  PATH FORM CORRECTED AGAIN (2026-09-10, second pass).

  MGL path rules, from MiSTer's own docs (mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/mgl):
    <rbf>       "Relative path to the core's RBF file from the SD root, excluding
                 its file extension" -- so it resolves under /media/fat ONLY. A core
                 sitting on a USB drive CANNOT be referenced by an MGL.
    <file path> "Path to game file relative to the core's games folder" -- documented
                 examples are bare (dummy.chd, cds/dummy.iso). With <setname>System573
                 the games folder is games/System573, searched ACROSS storages, so a
                 bare filename works on SD and USB alike. That is why this form is
                 preferable to the absolute /media/fat/... paths this file first used.

  History, so nobody repeats it: the original absolute /media/fat paths silently loaded
  NOTHING when the games live on USB (the core then autoloaded games/PSX/boot.rom -- the
  consumer Sony BIOS -- and showed the PlayStation logo). The first correction made them
  games/System573/<file>, which is wrong too: relative to the games folder that means
  games/System573/games/System573/<file>. Bare filenames are the documented form.

  Entries with paths OUTSIDE the games folder (the saves/ slot below, where present) are
  left as-is and are NOT verified against the docs.
-->
<!--
  konam80s (Konami 80's AC Special) -- a CD-INSTALLER game, the 2nd CD-install
  title and the FIRST X76F041-cassette title on the core. Reuses exactly the
  hypbbc2p (game #2) path: standalone console core (is_arcade_type=0), BLANK 16MB
  flash + BLANK 8KB NVRAM, the CD in the S1 (CUECHD) slot, and the AUTHENTIC
  security cassette on ioctl index 4. On first boot with Boot Device = CD-ROM the
  BIOS runs the CD installer (re-programs the onboard flash from the disc) + writes
  an installed signature to NVRAM, then the game runs from flash.

  CASSETTE: konam80s uses an X76F041 (512B + separate read/write/config passwords)
  -- a DIFFERENT chip than hypbbc2p's X76F100. The 548-byte .u1 latches as X76F041
  per emu.sv's size tiers (>=256 -> F041). Like every cassette title, it REQUIRES
  the AUTHENTIC dump: stage the real gc826ea.u1 as games/System573/konam80s.u1.
  The BIOS boot-time SIGNATURE check (the -11N wall) needs authentic-cassette data
  not derivable from plaintext -- see docs/2026-06-12-game2-hypbbc2p-cd-install.md
  + tools/gen_seccart_u1.py. (gc826ea.u1 is MAME-"BAD_DUMP"/NEEDS REDUMP but is the
  best-available authentic set -- same status as hypbbc2p's gx908ja.u1, which worked.)

  TEST PROCEDURE (de-confounded: warm-reboot, /proc/uptime < 60s, ONE load):
    1. Launch this .mgl.  2. OSD set "573 Boot Device" -> CD-ROM (status O[93]).
    3. Let the installer run (CD -> flash; lengthy).
    4. After install, set "573 Boot Device" -> Flash ROM and reload to run the game.
  Judge every result with frame_diff, not vision. konam80s is the FIRST HW exercise
  of the X76F041 model (sim-proven; rtl/x76f041.v) -- watch for cassette-auth faults.

  Requires: _Console/Konami_System_573.rbf + games/System573/{573bios.bin,
  flash16m_blank.bin, nvram8k_blank.bin, konam80s.u1 (= real gc826ea.u1), konam80s.chd}.
-->
<mistergamedescription>
  <rbf>_Console/Konami_System_573</rbf>
  <setname>System573</setname>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="0" path="573bios.bin"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="2" path="flash16m_blank.bin"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="3" path="nvram8k_blank.bin"/>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="4" path="konam80s.u1"/>
  <file delay="2" type="s" index="1" path="konam80s.chd"/>
  <!-- FLASH PERSISTENCE (slot 4): see hypbbc2p_console.mgl for the full rationale.
       Auto-created on first write-back; LOADed over the blank on later launches.
       *** PARENT VERIFY ON HW (gate-0 RISK R4): a .mgl type="s" at a not-yet-existent
       saves/ path must trigger Main pre-allocate auto-create; fallback = one
       user_io_file_mount(savepath, 4, 1, 16*1024*1024) in the PSX support file. -->
  <file delay="3" type="s" index="4" path="saves/System573/konam80s.sav"/>
  <reset delay="1"/>
</mistergamedescription>
